{
  "description": "The Fly GraphQL schema marks nothing sensitive, so every AddOn selection returned its credentials as plain values that print and log. `password` is the add-on password, `publicUrl` embeds it (e.g. `redis://default:<password>@…`), and `environment` is the JSON object of variables Fly sets as secrets on the attached app (flyctl `setSecretsFromExtension` in internal/command/extensions/core/core.go writes each key with `SetSecrets`); for a Tigris add-on that is `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`. GraphQL convert inlines `AddOn` into one shape per selecting operation (addOn, addOns, organization.addOns, createAddOn, updateAddOn, resetAddOnPassword), so each copy is marked. `environment` is a JSON scalar and decodes to Redacted<unknown> as a whole.",
